WEBVTT

00:05.797 --> 00:07.882
[theme music playing]

00:15.306 --> 00:16.808
BASED ON THE KINGDOM OF THE GODS

00:22.647 --> 00:24.649
[suspenseful music playing]

00:58.850 --> 00:59.684
[clang]

01:15.116 --> 01:16.326
[growling]

01:53.488 --> 01:55.156
[second queen] As you ordered,

01:55.949 --> 01:57.659
all the gates have been sealed.

01:58.952 --> 01:59.786
However,

02:00.495 --> 02:03.581
do you really plan to give up on
the entire region of Gyeongsang?

02:04.165 --> 02:06.709
It does not compare to Jeolla,
which is lush and abundant,

02:06.793 --> 02:09.921
but do you really plan to give up
all the grains

02:10.463 --> 02:12.507
the subjects of Gyeongsang offer up?

02:16.761 --> 02:19.013
Do you regard power...

02:21.766 --> 02:24.185
only as the means of coveting money?

02:29.065 --> 02:30.441
How many dead bodies...

02:32.068 --> 02:34.362
do you think are there
at the bottom of this pond?

02:36.406 --> 02:40.076
Bringing the day
when no one can say a word about

02:40.994 --> 02:44.205
how many bodies I have dumped
in this pond.

02:45.707 --> 02:47.292
That is what power is for.

02:50.628 --> 02:51.838
I will use that power...

02:53.047 --> 02:54.883
to protect you, Father.

02:55.383 --> 02:58.386
I am the one
who placed that power in your hand.

03:01.097 --> 03:04.058
I am also the one
who can take it away from you at any time.

03:07.520 --> 03:09.355
Do not open the gates

03:10.857 --> 03:12.775
until I give the orders.

03:18.823 --> 03:20.241
What about the Crown Prince?

03:24.704 --> 03:28.583
The Crown Prince is still alive
in Gyeongsang.

03:30.210 --> 03:33.546
Do you plan to let him be?

03:40.970 --> 03:41.971
I will...

03:44.057 --> 03:45.600
kill the Crown Prince.

03:48.478 --> 03:49.687
I will...

03:51.564 --> 03:53.608
kill him with my own hands.

04:22.470 --> 04:24.097
- Lord Ahn!
- [door closes]

04:32.063 --> 04:33.606
Hand over the Crown Prince.

04:34.315 --> 04:37.110
Cho Hak-ju has closed Mungyeong Saejae.

04:37.527 --> 04:40.238
We need the Crown Prince
if we are to get it open again.

04:40.655 --> 04:42.282
Where is he?

04:43.992 --> 04:45.660
[approaching footsteps]

04:48.288 --> 04:49.289
My lord,

04:50.039 --> 04:51.165
they have arrived.

04:55.336 --> 04:57.255
Sure, I will grant your request.

04:58.464 --> 05:00.508
I will let you take His Royal Highness.

05:09.851 --> 05:11.269
[Mu-yeong] Your Royal Highness.

05:11.853 --> 05:13.271
You cannot trust anyone.

05:16.733 --> 05:18.067
We must leave this place.

05:23.323 --> 05:24.324
Your Royal Highness.

05:24.824 --> 05:27.493
[man] Crown Prince Lee Chang,
come out at once!

05:32.915 --> 05:34.500
[door creaks]

05:44.302 --> 05:45.928
You have come a long way.

05:47.638 --> 05:49.599
It is time to return to Hanyang.

05:50.391 --> 05:51.642
[approaching footsteps]

06:03.279 --> 06:04.864
Are they not palace guards?

06:05.365 --> 06:07.200
Thank you for guarding the criminal.

06:08.534 --> 06:09.911
As per the King's command,

06:11.204 --> 06:12.747
I shall escort him to prison.

06:12.830 --> 06:14.540
Bind the traitor!

06:15.041 --> 06:16.209
[servants] Yes, sir.

06:16.876 --> 06:18.586
How dare you?

06:18.669 --> 06:19.587
[Ahn Hyeon] Who?

06:20.671 --> 06:22.340
Who is the traitor?

06:24.801 --> 06:26.135
A palace guard,

06:27.512 --> 06:29.722
who should serve the nation and the King,

06:31.641 --> 06:35.061
gave into his personal greed
and became Cho Hak-ju's lapdog.

06:37.563 --> 06:40.358
For oppressing the Crown Prince,
the heir to the throne,

06:41.484 --> 06:44.195
and disrupting the core values
of this nation,

06:46.531 --> 06:47.907
you deserve to be executed.

06:50.118 --> 06:51.035
Execute him!

06:53.162 --> 06:54.872
[swords rasping]

06:56.707 --> 06:58.126
What do you think you are doing?

06:59.502 --> 07:00.711
[grunting]

07:04.590 --> 07:06.259
[yells, grunts]

07:13.099 --> 07:17.520
Sangju is my hometown
and where I currently reside.

07:18.855 --> 07:21.899
I urge you, Your Royal Highness,
to rest peacefully for tonight.

07:22.400 --> 07:23.359
[sighs]

07:24.110 --> 07:25.945
There is no time to rest.

07:26.028 --> 07:27.238
You should rest

07:28.573 --> 07:30.241
and let your body recover.

07:30.867 --> 07:31.868
How else...

07:32.869 --> 07:36.205
will you fight the chief palace guard?

07:37.415 --> 07:39.041
What do you mean?

07:41.043 --> 07:42.128
Yesterday,

07:43.421 --> 07:46.340
a homing pigeon
delivered this secret letter

07:47.467 --> 07:48.885
from the chief palace guard.

07:50.803 --> 07:52.930
He said Your Royal Highness
was headed this way

07:54.515 --> 07:58.311
and that I should lock you up
until he arrives.

07:59.812 --> 08:01.939
The chief palace guard
could not have known

08:02.356 --> 08:03.941
that I was headed here.

08:07.528 --> 08:08.613
[sighs]

08:08.696 --> 08:10.156
One of your companions...

08:11.240 --> 08:14.118
is Cho Hak-ju's mole.

08:15.203 --> 08:16.078
Thus,

08:17.663 --> 08:22.126
you must not let anyone know
what we just discussed.

08:29.217 --> 08:30.635
[groaning]

08:31.219 --> 08:32.303
[grunting]

08:36.182 --> 08:40.311
None of you shall survive.
Not a single one.

08:41.729 --> 08:45.316
Not only you, but your families...

08:47.902 --> 08:49.987
will be trapped in Gyeongsang,

08:51.906 --> 08:54.033
catch the disease, and be decapitated.

08:57.870 --> 08:58.913
[grunts]

09:02.792 --> 09:04.168
[magistrate] What have you done?

09:04.252 --> 09:07.004
How could you massacre palace guards
delivering the King's command?

09:07.088 --> 09:09.757
Do you think Lord Cho Hak-ju
will let you get away with this?

09:11.008 --> 09:14.178
He will accuse you of treason
and turn Sangju into a bloodbath!

09:14.262 --> 09:16.556
Cho Hak-ju has already abandoned Sangju.

09:16.639 --> 09:19.600
He has abandoned not only Sangju,
but also the east and west regions

09:19.684 --> 09:21.978
of Gyeongsang and the people therein.

09:22.770 --> 09:23.938
What do you mean?

09:24.355 --> 09:26.065
Do you think all those soldiers

09:26.148 --> 09:28.526
blocked off Mungyeong Saejae
just to stop me?

09:32.697 --> 09:34.907
My lord, we have a big problem.

09:35.324 --> 09:37.326
[crowd shouting]

09:51.799 --> 09:54.468
Yangsan, Gyeongju, Daegu,
Hapcheon, Changnyeong...

09:54.885 --> 09:56.512
They came from various parts

09:56.596 --> 09:58.514
of the southern region
to escape the epidemic.

09:58.973 --> 10:01.475
All of them were hit by the epidemic?

10:01.559 --> 10:05.021
If Changnyeong was already hit,
the infected will get here in two days

10:05.688 --> 10:07.273
or as soon as tonight.

10:07.982 --> 10:11.360
[sighs] You must open the gate
and let them in.

10:11.444 --> 10:15.364
If all parts of Gyeongsang were hit,
there will be more and more refugees.

10:15.781 --> 10:18.576
How are we going to house
and feed them all?

10:19.452 --> 10:21.662
Once we run out of food,
they will start looting.

10:21.746 --> 10:23.331
There will be mayhem inside the fortress.

10:23.414 --> 10:26.667
Then do you plan to sit back
and watch them die?

10:29.670 --> 10:31.672
[crowd clamoring]

10:33.007 --> 10:36.093
[crowd wailing]

10:39.513 --> 10:40.890
If you do not open the gate now,

10:40.973 --> 10:43.351
people of Sangju outside the fortress
will also be in danger.

10:43.434 --> 10:44.393
Open the gate.

10:45.353 --> 10:46.937
We cannot open the gate.

10:48.064 --> 10:50.066
At least the people inside must survive.

10:51.734 --> 10:55.363
I am sure Cho Hak-ju said the same thing
when he closed Mungyeong Saejae.

10:56.322 --> 10:57.948
That at least they must survive.

10:58.449 --> 11:00.409
This is a small sacrifice
for the greater good.

11:00.868 --> 11:03.329
Who are you to decide whom to sacrifice?

11:04.455 --> 11:07.541
If you lock the gate, those outside
will catch the disease and die.

11:07.625 --> 11:10.461
The people inside will be trapped
and die of starvation.

11:12.380 --> 11:14.006
I am the magistrate of Sangju!

11:14.090 --> 11:14.965
No.

11:15.883 --> 11:18.135
You are no longer qualified
to run this place.

11:19.011 --> 11:21.013
- What?
- I cannot let everyone die

11:21.097 --> 11:22.973
because of an incompetent official.

11:23.057 --> 11:26.143
I will protect Sangju and the people
from now on.

11:27.520 --> 11:29.021
By what right?

11:31.691 --> 11:33.109
I am the Crown Prince.

11:35.236 --> 11:37.405
I strip you of the title
from this moment forth!

11:39.949 --> 11:41.617
It is the Crown Prince's command.

11:42.076 --> 11:43.411
Escort the magistrate out.

11:43.828 --> 11:44.829
Lord Ahn,

11:45.663 --> 11:46.997
you cannot do this.

11:48.541 --> 11:50.126
You will regret this.

11:55.005 --> 11:56.006
Move aside!

12:01.345 --> 12:02.388
What will you do?

12:03.139 --> 12:04.724
Even if we open the gate,

12:05.516 --> 12:08.686
the inside of the fortress is not spacious
enough to shelter the refugees

12:09.353 --> 12:10.938
as well as the people outside.

12:11.939 --> 12:13.023
You are correct.

12:14.358 --> 12:16.277
It cannot house everyone.

12:18.487 --> 12:19.864
If we are to save everyone,

12:20.656 --> 12:22.742
we must protect the entirety of Sangju.

12:23.159 --> 12:25.411
The infected will soon come charging in.

12:26.245 --> 12:27.830
How can we protect all of Sangju?

12:30.416 --> 12:33.544
The diseased are corpses during the day
and come alive only at night.

12:33.627 --> 12:35.129
They also fear water and fire.

12:36.297 --> 12:38.632
If we take advantage of that,
we can stop them.

12:45.556 --> 12:49.018
The south of Sangju
is surrounded by water.

12:51.103 --> 12:52.897
If we guard both Byeongseong Stream

12:54.023 --> 12:55.608
and Unpo Wetland against them,

12:56.275 --> 12:57.443
we all can...

12:59.069 --> 13:00.279
survive.

13:01.822 --> 13:03.657
[crowd clamoring]

13:09.455 --> 13:11.457
[cheering]

13:39.151 --> 13:40.152
[grunts]

14:01.882 --> 14:02.967
[clears throat]

14:03.050 --> 14:06.220
You cannot do this.
How could you tell noblemen to bear arms?

14:06.303 --> 14:07.596
This is nonsense.

14:07.680 --> 14:09.473
It is the Crown Prince's command.

14:09.557 --> 14:11.725
[men grumbling]

14:12.685 --> 14:17.690
[scoffs] We should be holding books,
not something like this.

14:20.985 --> 14:21.986
[sighs]

14:23.237 --> 14:24.613
[metal clanging]

15:04.695 --> 15:06.697
[indistinct chatter]

15:40.272 --> 15:41.982
[grunting]

15:44.401 --> 15:46.153
Okay, a little more.

15:47.071 --> 15:48.155
This is tiring.

15:48.781 --> 15:49.907
Okay, you should go.

15:53.994 --> 15:55.579
[servant] I will check the perimeter.

15:56.789 --> 15:57.915
[horse neighs]

15:57.998 --> 15:59.041
Giddyap.

16:12.137 --> 16:14.890
[court lady] I think the baby will be born
by the end of today.

16:15.641 --> 16:17.601
- Will it be a boy?
- We are not sure--

16:17.685 --> 16:19.895
Report to me only when a baby boy is born.

16:20.312 --> 16:21.522
Yes, Your Majesty.

16:22.606 --> 16:23.983
[rain pattering]

16:24.608 --> 16:25.734
[woman groans]

16:25.818 --> 16:28.153
[groaning intensifies]

16:28.237 --> 16:30.322
[woman screaming]

16:34.451 --> 16:35.369
[grunts]

16:38.956 --> 16:40.207
[screaming]

16:41.208 --> 16:43.877
[screaming intensifies]

16:44.962 --> 16:47.464
[crying] Mom!

16:52.261 --> 16:54.471
[baby crying]

16:54.555 --> 16:55.514
The baby is here!

16:55.597 --> 16:58.600
Thank goodness. She has been
in so much pain since last night.

16:58.684 --> 17:01.812
I know. It must have been so hard for her.

17:01.895 --> 17:02.980
[baby stops crying]

17:20.164 --> 17:22.332
It is cold outside. Return to your rooms.

17:22.416 --> 17:25.794
The baby stopped crying.
Is something wrong?

17:27.755 --> 17:29.757
Both the mother and the baby are safe.

17:29.840 --> 17:33.093
She is nursing the baby now, so go back.

17:37.639 --> 17:40.267
Is it a boy or a girl?

17:42.936 --> 17:44.146
It is a girl.

17:44.646 --> 17:47.316
- Gosh.
- Why does it have to be a girl?

17:47.399 --> 17:49.026
Who cares if it is a girl?

17:49.109 --> 17:51.236
It does not matter
as long as the baby is healthy.

18:17.805 --> 18:20.599
[gasps] Darn it. Oh, no.

18:20.682 --> 18:21.767
You are so...

18:26.021 --> 18:26.855
[sighs]

18:27.689 --> 18:29.733
Oh. Thank goodness.

18:30.234 --> 18:32.361
It did not damage Her Majesty's robe.

18:32.444 --> 18:33.445
Thank goodness.

18:33.862 --> 18:37.366
If you had left a single stain on it,
it would have turned into a pile of ashes.

18:37.449 --> 18:38.534
What do you mean?

18:39.118 --> 18:41.036
One time,

18:41.120 --> 18:43.831
I saw them burning
Her Majesty's precious silk robe.

18:45.082 --> 18:46.250
Really?

18:46.333 --> 18:47.251
Yes, for real.

18:47.751 --> 18:50.254
The head court lady burned it herself.

18:50.963 --> 18:53.841
It only had a tiny blood stain on it.

18:54.550 --> 18:55.717
What a waste.

18:56.510 --> 18:57.469
My gosh.

18:58.053 --> 19:01.306
I could die a happy girl
if I could wear something like this once.

19:01.390 --> 19:04.393
[sucks teeth] What could lowly girls
like us possibly expect?

19:05.769 --> 19:07.354
[sighs] We shall go.

19:07.938 --> 19:08.814
Okay.

19:16.738 --> 19:17.614
[both gasp]

19:17.698 --> 19:19.199
[both] Your Majesty.

19:23.453 --> 19:25.247
If you are done cleaning, you may leave.

19:25.789 --> 19:26.957
[both] Yes, my lady.

19:33.797 --> 19:35.674
[water splashing]

19:46.602 --> 19:47.728
My lady,

19:48.353 --> 19:50.856
will I really serve Her Majesty?

19:51.773 --> 19:54.484
Why someone lowly like me,
instead of a court lady?

19:54.902 --> 19:57.613
Do not speak,
and focus on serving Her Majesty.

20:27.100 --> 20:28.727
Why are you so slow?

20:28.810 --> 20:30.062
My apologies, Your Majesty.

20:49.957 --> 20:51.041
[maid gasps]

20:52.709 --> 20:53.919
[court lady] How dare you?

20:56.004 --> 20:57.256
[maid shudders]

21:15.774 --> 21:17.025
What do you think?

21:17.943 --> 21:20.362
My baby looks very healthy, does he not?

21:26.326 --> 21:27.953
Please have mercy, Your Majesty!

21:51.018 --> 21:51.977
Oh.

21:53.770 --> 21:55.439
[panting]

21:56.106 --> 21:59.192
- My lord, I shall carry that for you.
- There is no need to. Just go.

22:06.742 --> 22:07.701
What do you think?

22:09.161 --> 22:10.787
This is plenty, is it not?

22:14.166 --> 22:16.043
[laughing]

22:20.714 --> 22:21.923
[Beom-pal sighs]

22:26.511 --> 22:27.512
[Seo-bi gasps]

22:29.097 --> 22:30.766
You are incredible.

22:30.849 --> 22:32.434
[laughing]

22:32.517 --> 22:35.520
How did you pick nothing but weeds?

22:35.979 --> 22:36.897
What?

22:38.023 --> 22:40.984
What? Look closely.

22:41.651 --> 22:43.653
I only picked what you told me to pick.

22:44.196 --> 22:47.866
You must be tired. You should rest.

22:47.949 --> 22:49.201
[stammers] But...

22:49.576 --> 22:51.787
I will go and pick it myself.

22:51.870 --> 22:54.581
But... what do you mean I should rest?

22:56.083 --> 22:57.209
[Beom-pal groans]

22:57.292 --> 22:59.544
How can a man rest
when everyone else is working?

23:00.128 --> 23:01.088
Seo-bi!

23:01.755 --> 23:04.841
[Beom-pal groans]
Is that not more than enough?

23:06.259 --> 23:08.678
There are more medicinal herbs
that I must find.

23:09.513 --> 23:12.265
What more are you looking for?

23:13.433 --> 23:14.893
False lily of the valley.

23:14.976 --> 23:17.354
His Royal Highness's wounds
have not healed yet.

23:18.146 --> 23:19.898
I need that plant.

23:21.316 --> 23:23.276
So, it is for the Crown Prince.

23:23.902 --> 23:24.903
[Beom-pal grunts]

23:26.571 --> 23:27.572
Seo-bi.

23:28.782 --> 23:30.367
Seo-bi. [grunts]

23:30.909 --> 23:32.702
I am hurt as well.

23:33.537 --> 23:36.498
You got hurt while running away.

23:39.418 --> 23:40.460
[Beom-pal sighs]

23:42.587 --> 23:44.297
No... You...

23:44.381 --> 23:46.258
You cannot go that way.

23:46.341 --> 23:49.386
[pants] The magistrate's office
said that path is dangerous

23:49.803 --> 23:52.097
and strictly forbids entering it.

23:53.390 --> 23:55.725
[Seo-bi]
It is not like there are tigers there.

23:55.809 --> 23:57.727
What is dangerous about it?

23:58.186 --> 24:00.480
Who knows?
It is called Frozen Valley or something.

24:00.564 --> 24:02.691
Maybe it is haunted or something.

24:02.774 --> 24:04.484
We should go back.

24:06.153 --> 24:07.696
What did you just say?

24:07.779 --> 24:09.322
What? What do you mean?

24:10.782 --> 24:12.492
Did you say, "Frozen Valley"?

24:13.034 --> 24:13.869
Yes.

24:14.369 --> 24:16.830
That valley up there is
called Frozen Valley.

24:18.165 --> 24:19.749
[Beom-pal panting]

24:22.752 --> 24:24.629
Wait. Wait.

24:25.297 --> 24:28.383
Why is she so fearless?

24:29.593 --> 24:30.469
Well,

24:31.553 --> 24:33.180
that is her charm.

24:33.638 --> 24:34.890
[pants] Seo-bi.

24:36.224 --> 24:37.184
[Beom-pal grunts]

24:41.771 --> 24:44.024
Wait, Seo-bi.

24:46.067 --> 24:48.403
- [wind gusting]
- [leaves rustling]

25:06.505 --> 25:07.964
[Beom-pal grunting]

25:11.718 --> 25:13.512
[chimes ringing]

25:17.098 --> 25:20.727
It is chilly.
It already feels like winter here.

25:21.478 --> 25:23.230
[Beom-pal panting]

25:24.481 --> 25:27.025
A place where it is foggy
all year round...

25:30.862 --> 25:32.155
[chimes rattle]

25:32.239 --> 25:34.449
Wait, Seo... Seo-bi.

25:35.784 --> 25:36.952
Hold on.

25:39.913 --> 25:40.956
Seo... Seo-bi!

25:43.375 --> 25:44.459
Seo... Seo-bi.

25:45.460 --> 25:46.920
[Beom-pal panting]

25:48.213 --> 25:49.172
[groans]

25:50.924 --> 25:52.092
[chimes rattle]

26:00.725 --> 26:02.936
[Beom-pal whimpering]

26:03.019 --> 26:05.438
It is too cold! It is so cold!

26:12.779 --> 26:14.239
[panting]

26:20.287 --> 26:21.663
The resurrection plant...

26:21.746 --> 26:23.164
[panting]

26:24.708 --> 26:26.501
What? What did you say?

26:28.628 --> 26:29.838
[Beom-pal groaning]

26:30.672 --> 26:32.132
This is the plant.

26:34.092 --> 26:36.595
This plant brought the dead back to life.

26:38.763 --> 26:41.391
This is the plant
that brought the dead back to life!

26:52.944 --> 26:54.529
What is that?

27:04.831 --> 27:06.833
[chimes rattling]

27:13.548 --> 27:14.799
- [thud]
- [both gasp]

27:21.222 --> 27:22.432
[gunshot]

27:22.515 --> 27:24.059
[amused gasp]

27:25.352 --> 27:26.645
When aiming a gun,

27:27.354 --> 27:30.023
you must keep the muzzle, the barrel,
and the arm in a straight line

27:30.106 --> 27:31.149
as much as you can.

27:32.067 --> 27:33.485
He is good with guns.

27:34.194 --> 27:36.363
[Deok-seong]
He used to be a member of Chakho.

27:38.031 --> 27:40.241
He's the one from Sumang Village
that I spoke of.

27:50.543 --> 27:51.586
[Yeong-sin] Fire!

27:51.670 --> 27:52.962
[gunshots]

27:55.048 --> 27:56.341
Do you know him?

27:58.468 --> 27:59.552
No.

28:00.595 --> 28:01.846
I do not know him.

28:09.854 --> 28:10.939
[Yeong-sin] Fire!

28:11.022 --> 28:12.065
[gunshots]

28:17.737 --> 28:19.239
Everyone, listen up!

28:19.656 --> 28:21.282
The sun will set soon!

28:22.242 --> 28:24.244
Check your surroundings one more time!

28:24.911 --> 28:28.206
Do not leave your post for any reason!

28:28.957 --> 28:30.917
- Do you understand?
- [men] Yes, sir!

28:33.002 --> 28:34.713
[men grunting]

28:36.548 --> 28:38.007
[officer] Cast off the boats!

28:38.091 --> 28:42.762
Two! One! Two!

28:43.722 --> 28:44.681
One!

28:45.640 --> 28:46.891
Two!

28:48.101 --> 28:50.103
[tense music playing]

29:18.590 --> 29:20.091
[wind gusting]

29:22.761 --> 29:25.138
The ones who went on the reconnaissance
have not yet returned.

30:06.805 --> 30:08.097
[rumbling]

30:10.558 --> 30:12.060
[guard] We have arrived, my lord.

30:24.697 --> 30:25.740
[horse snorting]

30:29.994 --> 30:31.412
THE FIRST GATE OF MUNGYEONG SAEJAE

30:31.496 --> 30:32.956
Welcome, Chief State Councillor.

30:41.422 --> 30:42.632
What is the status?

30:43.049 --> 30:44.801
Sangju is still safe from the epidemic.

30:47.011 --> 30:48.137
[thud]

30:48.847 --> 30:50.557
- [thud]
- [horse neighs]

30:51.140 --> 30:52.725
[horse whinnying]

30:56.771 --> 30:58.231
[thudding continues]

31:01.568 --> 31:03.444
[thudding intensifies]

31:17.417 --> 31:18.543
Your Royal Highness.

31:20.003 --> 31:23.131
The sun will rise soon, and we only need
to hang on a little longer.

31:26.050 --> 31:27.093
[sighs]

31:31.973 --> 31:33.016
Your Royal Highness.

31:43.985 --> 31:45.111
[men gasp]

31:57.749 --> 31:58.875
[horse neighs]

32:02.295 --> 32:04.631
It's the horse of the servant
who was out to survey the area.

32:05.506 --> 32:06.591
[officer] Let it through.

32:45.964 --> 32:47.757
The blood has not dried yet.

32:50.051 --> 32:51.469
They will be here soon.

33:06.567 --> 33:07.944
[explosion]

33:14.617 --> 33:16.494
The signal fire has been lit.
Sound the drums!

33:16.577 --> 33:18.913
[drum thumping]

33:29.799 --> 33:31.801
[tense music playing]

34:05.918 --> 34:07.128
Please rise.

34:23.394 --> 34:26.272
It is very cold outside.
You should get inside, my lord.

34:32.111 --> 34:33.988
[birds squawking]

35:08.940 --> 35:10.733
- It is the sun!
- The sun is up!

35:18.324 --> 35:19.450
[sighs]

35:31.546 --> 35:34.924
We must prepare for tonight,
so I will tell them to get some rest.

35:39.971 --> 35:41.722
- Everyone, come in!
- [men cheering]

35:41.806 --> 35:44.308
- We made it!
- Let us pull out for today!

35:44.392 --> 35:46.227
[indistinct chatter]

35:55.987 --> 35:58.948
[men] One, two. One, two.

36:00.950 --> 36:04.162
Now that the sun has risen,
let us get some sleep.

36:04.245 --> 36:05.913
Let us eat some delicious food!

36:05.997 --> 36:06.914
Let us go.

36:16.299 --> 36:18.134
Do you think it is over?

36:20.845 --> 36:24.140
Pack up quickly,
and prepare for the evening!

36:24.223 --> 36:25.391
[men] Yes, sir!

36:30.938 --> 36:32.940
[birds squawking]

36:57.423 --> 36:59.425
[distant growling]

36:59.508 --> 37:01.219
[Beom-pal whimpers]

37:04.222 --> 37:06.599
[Beom-pal]
How are they out during the day?

37:11.979 --> 37:14.815
It was not the sun.

37:17.109 --> 37:18.527
It was the temperature.

37:23.115 --> 37:25.117
[rumbling]

38:32.435 --> 38:34.437
[distant growling]

38:39.859 --> 38:40.943
[growling]

38:50.369 --> 38:52.204
[growling intensifies]

39:05.885 --> 39:07.720
[growling]

39:21.776 --> 39:23.778
[theme music playing]

43:14.925 --> 43:16.594
[music ends]
